From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:51:17 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ASoC: samsung: exynos9610-a50: add the RT5665 codec on
 UAIF0

Add what the stock vogue-rt5665 machine driver gives the card for the
RT5665 codec on UAIF0 and the board:

- UAIF0 hw_params/hw_free: keep the UAIF0 bit clock running (Q-channel
  disabled through set_tristate) while a stream uses it and lock the
  codec PLL1 to BCLK1, system clock 512 fs, as stock.
- The stock board widgets (VOUTPUT, HEADSETMIC, MAINMIC, SUBMIC,
  RECEIVER, HEADPHONE, SPEAKER, BLUETOOTH, FM IN, call paths) for the
  DT routing, their pin switches, and the "Sound Wakelock" control on a
  wakeup source instead of the Android wake_lock.

Left out: the stock headset jack (Samsung-only JD1+JD2 detection and
SAR buttons), "ABOX VSS State" (voice, M11) and the per-widget log-only
event handlers. Kconfig selects the mainline RT5665 driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
